S={}
S[1]="Part one. This older red car hauler just rolled into Car Hauler Repair Houston, and at first glance it shows every year it has worked. There's corrosion at the joints, the decks are due for replacement, and the front section needs serious attention. But once we got underneath and inspected the frame, we found what matters most: a solid foundation that is absolutely worth saving, which changes the whole plan. Instead of patching problems one by one, we're taking this trailer through a complete restoration, from structural welding to new decks, sandblasting and fresh paint. Follow along as we bring this hauler back to work."
S[2]="Part two. With a solid foundation confirmed, the first stage is structural welding. Years of work and weather left corrosion at key joints across this red car hauler, and those joints carry the load every time the trailer is loaded and on the road. Our team went through the frame joint by joint and welded the corroded areas back to full strength. This is the stage most people never see once the paint goes on, but it's the work that decides how long a trailer will stay in service. Strong joints come first, and everything else in this rebuild is built on top of them."
S[3]="Part three. With the joints welded, we moved on to the decks, the parts that take the most abuse every single day. The old decks on this red car hauler had served their time, so we removed them and installed new ones, including the front section of the trailer. We build decks like these in our shop, and not just one style: we make all kinds of car hauler decks to fit different trailers and different jobs. Every position on this hauler now has a solid surface again. Want to see more of our decks up close? Check out our page for the details."
S[4]="Part four. Once all the welding and deck work was complete, this car hauler went into sandblasting. Blasting strips away old coatings, rust and surface contamination, exposing clean steel so the new finish can actually bond instead of sitting on top of old problems. After blasting, the trailer was painted, and that fresh finish does more than make it look good in the yard. It protects the steel we just repaired and helps keep corrosion from coming back to the joints we welded earlier. This is where years of wear disappear, and the hauler finally starts looking like the trailer its owner remembers."
S[5]="Part five. After about a month in our shop, this car hauler is in the final stretch. The last details are what make a restoration complete, so we replaced the bulbs, making sure the trailer is visible and ready for the road. From a tired older hauler with a solid foundation to welded joints, new decks, sandblasting and fresh paint, it's been a full transformation. Now it's just waiting for its owner to come pick it up and put it back to work, hopefully any day now. Need your car hauler restored? Contact Car Hauler Repair Houston."
import re
# how numbers are actually spoken in the VO (checked by ASR) — display keeps the digits
SPOKEN={"2007":"two thousand seven"}
def say(t):
    for k,v in SPOKEN.items(): t=re.sub(r"\b"+k+r"\b",v,t)
    return t
HOOK={}   # key -> aligned-word index where the mid-video hook starts (marker [HOOK 2] in the text files)
def norm(t): return [w for w in re.sub(r"[^a-z' ]"," ",say(t).lower().replace("—"," ")).split()]
S[4]="Part four. With the welding and deck work complete, this car hauler was prepared for sandblasting. The entire trailer was blasted down to clean bare steel, stripping away old coatings, rust and surface contamination so every coat that follows goes onto a proper surface. Before any paint went on, our team masked and taped off every element that needed protection. Then came the primer, the brown-orange coat, which seals the fresh steel and gives the paint a strong surface to bond to. The final stage is the red top coat, laid over the primer for a durable, professional finish. This is where years of wear disappear, and the hauler finally starts looking like the trailer its owner remembers."

# ===== standalone videos (key = name, VO file in voiceover/) =====
S["decks"]="At Car Hauler Repair Houston, deck work is a big part of what we do. Decks take more abuse than almost any other part of a car hauler, and every vehicle that's loaded and unloaded wears them down a little more. Damaged decks slow down loading and put the cars you haul at risk, so it pays to fix them before they fail. We repair damaged decks and build new ones in our shop, working in both steel and aluminum, from perforated deck sections to complete deck replacements, and right now we're also building aluminum ramps. Whatever style your trailer runs, we build decks to fit it. Want to see more of our deck work? Check out our page, or contact Car Hauler Repair Houston."
VO={4:"part4_v2.mp3","decks":"decks.mp3","miller":"miller.mp3","sandblast":"sandblast.mp3"}
S["miller"]="This 2007 Miller seven-car hauler came into Car Hauler Repair Houston with worn-out hinge points. The bushings were broken, several hinges were worn far past their service life, and the platform was badly damaged, so it no longer operated the way it should. Our team replaced the bushings and partially replaced the hinges that were too worn to keep, restoring the pivot points that every platform movement depends on. Worn bushings and hinges don't fix themselves, and the longer they're ignored, the more damage they do to the rest of the trailer. Now this Miller's platform is ready to work correctly again. Need hinge or bushing repair? Contact Car Hauler Repair Houston."
# as actually voiced (ASR-checked 2026-09-22): cylinder clause dropped, "fully prepared", "ready for the next stage"
S["sandblast"]="Sandblasting is one of the most demanding jobs we do at Car Hauler Repair Houston, and it's the step that decides how long the paint job lasts. Before blasting, the trailer is fully prepared. Then our team blasts the entire frame, cutting through old paint and rust until the whole trailer is down to bare gray steel, ready for the next stage. Next, every element that needs protection is masked and taped, and the trailer gets a coat of brown primer to seal the fresh metal. The final stage is the red top coat, laid over the primer for a clean, durable finish. Paint can only be as good as the surface underneath it. Contact Car Hauler Repair Houston for sandblasting and paint."

# ===== paint series 2026-09-22 (scripts/paint_series_0922.txt) =====
S['fullrefinish']="When an older car hauler needs more than a touch-up, Car Hauler Repair Houston takes the finish all the way back to bare metal. The trailer is stripped and sandblasted, removing old coatings and rust from the entire frame until only clean gray steel is left. That fresh steel is treated for corrosion and sealed with an industrial epoxy primer, the layer that holds everything that comes after it. Then the trailer is professionally painted with a durable industrial top coat, and a non-skid surface is added where it's needed. We don't hide problems under a quick coat of paint. We remove them, protect the steel, and send the trailer back to work. Bring your hauler to Car Hauler Repair Houston."
VO['fullrefinish']='fullrefinish.mp3'
S['primer']="Primer is the coat most people never notice, and it's one of the most important steps in any trailer restoration. On this car hauler, the frame was sandblasted down to bare gray steel first, because primer can only bond properly to a clean surface. Our team then sprayed the structure with a brown industrial epoxy primer, section by section, sealing the fresh metal before moisture and rust had a chance to come back. Every beam, post and deck support gets covered before any color goes on. Only after the primer is down does the red top coat follow. Skip this step, and even the best paint won't last. Ask Car Hauler Repair Houston about sandblasting and primer work."
VO['primer']='primer.mp3'
S['topcoat']='This is the moment a restoration finally becomes visible. After sandblasting and primer, this car hauler received its red top coat at Car Hauler Repair Houston, laid over every beam, post and deck section of the frame. We finish trailers with durable industrial or polyurethane coatings, made to stand up to heavy loads and daily work. A good top coat does more than make a trailer look new again. It protects the steel underneath and helps keep corrosion from coming back. From the upper decks down to the lower frame, the whole structure now carries one clean, even finish. If your hauler is ready for a fresh start, we can take it from bare steel to final coat.'
VO['topcoat']='topcoat.mp3'
S['nonskid']="The red paint is done, but this car hauler isn't finished yet. The next step is non-skid. First, our team masks off the freshly painted steel with tape, leaving open only the strips that will get the new surface. Then the non-skid coating is rolled on by hand, one section at a time, along the rails and edges of the trailer. The tape keeps every line clean, so the texture goes exactly where it belongs and the new paint stays untouched. The result is a sharp red finish with a textured surface built right into it. Small details like this are what separate a simple paint job from a real restoration. See more of our work on our page."
VO['nonskid']='nonskid.mp3'
S['fromabove']='From the air, you can see the full scope of a complete restoration. This car hauler was sandblasted, primed and repainted at Car Hauler Repair Houston, and every deck and beam now shares the same fresh red finish. Projects like this are handled from start to finish under one roof, from bare steel preparation and corrosion protection all the way to the final coat of paint. Our goal is never to cover problems with a temporary patch. We restore the structure, protect it against corrosion, and return the equipment to reliable working condition. Whether your trailer needs a single repair or a complete rebuild, our shop is equipped to handle the entire project. Car Hauler Repair Houston, Houston, Texas.'
VO['fromabove']='fromabove.mp3'
S['overview']="At Car Hauler Repair Houston, we work only on car haulers, from small repairs to complete rebuilds. We repair cracked frame rails, crossmembers, side beams and kingpin areas, and straighten frames that have lost their geometry. Our fabrication department works in steel, aluminum and stainless steel, building brackets, ramps and replacement sections. We replace decking, repair hydraulic systems from cylinders and hoses to pumps and PTO units, and handle wiring, lights, brakes and running gear. For full restorations, trailers are sandblasted, primed and painted. We work on Cottrell, Sun Country, Sun Valley, Wally-Mo, Boydstun, Miller and more, and we're a Cottrell Certified Warranty Repair Center. Everything your trailer needs, under one roof."
VO['overview']='overview.mp3'

# ===== 10 topics 2026-09-23 (scripts/topics_0923.txt) =====
S['hydraulics']='Almost every moving part on a car hauler runs on hydraulics, and when the system starts to fail, loading turns into a fight. At Car Hauler Repair Houston we repair and replace hydraulic cylinders, hoses, fittings, valves, pumps, electric motors, reservoirs and PTO systems. A cylinder that still has good steel can be rebuilt with new seals and components, and the ones that are past saving get replaced. We trace leaks back to the actual source, check the lines and the mounting points, and test the deck through its full travel before the trailer leaves. Hydraulic problems rarely fix themselves, and they get expensive when a deck drops or sticks. Hydraulics acting up? Bring the trailer to Car Hauler Repair Houston.'
VO['hydraulics']='hydraulics.mp3'
S['storage']='Storage compartments live in the worst spot on the trailer, right behind the wheels, where water, dirt and road spray hit them every single mile. On this hauler the compartment floor and its supports were eaten through, the doors no longer sat straight, and the box had stopped protecting anything stored inside. Our team stripped it back, cut out the rotted steel, and rebuilt the structure so the compartment sits square and closes properly again. It is a small part of a big trailer, and it is exactly the kind of repair people put off until the day their tools and chains are lying on the ground. Need a compartment rebuilt? Talk to Car Hauler Repair Houston.'
VO['storage']='storage.mp3'
S['corrosion']='Rust does not stop on its own. It works into seams, under skins and along the bottom rails, and by the time it shows on the outside, the steel underneath is usually thinner than it looks. At Car Hauler Repair Houston we cut out fatigued and damaged steel, fabricate replacement sections, and weld them back into the structure so the trailer carries load the way it was built to. Panels, rails, posts and skins all get treated the same way: remove what has failed, replace it with new material, and protect the repair against corrosion. Patching over rust only hides it for a season. Fighting rust on your trailer? Car Hauler Repair Houston can take care of it.'
VO['corrosion']='corrosion.mp3'
S['welding']='Every load a car hauler carries ends up in its welds. At Car Hauler Repair Houston we repair cracked and damaged frame rails, crossmembers, side beams and lower frames, and we reinforce high-stress areas with properly fitted structural plates, gussets and additional supports. Each repair starts with cleaning the steel and fitting the new piece tight, because a weld is only as good as what sits underneath it. We weld on the trailer and on the bench, wherever the repair is best done, and the finished joints go back into service carrying the same load as the original structure. Welds are not the place to save money. Got a cracked frame or a broken bracket? Call Car Hauler Repair Houston.'
VO['welding']='welding.mp3'
S['aluminum']='Aluminum is a different animal than steel, and it shows up all over a modern car hauler: ramps, deck sections, walkways and trim. Our fabrication department at Car Hauler Repair Houston works in steel, aluminum and stainless, so a damaged aluminum ramp does not mean waiting on a factory part that may not exist anymore. We build new sections in the shop, weld them to fit the trailer they belong on, and finish the edges so nothing catches a tire or a boot. Same trailer, same mounting points, new part. Running aluminum decks or ramps that have seen better days? Car Hauler Repair Houston builds them to fit.'
VO['aluminum']='aluminum.mp3'
S['shoptour']='This is where the work happens. Car Hauler Repair Houston is a shop built around one kind of equipment: car haulers. Inside, there is room to pull a trailer all the way in, lift the decks and work the frame from end to end, with the welding bays, the fabrication benches and the parts a rebuild needs in the same building. Outside, the yard holds the trailers waiting their turn and the ones that are already finished. Working under one roof is not about convenience, it is about control: the same team sees the trailer from the first cut to the last coat of paint. Come see the shop, or send us your trailer.'
VO['shoptour']='shoptour.mp3'
S['insideframe']='From the outside a five-car hauler looks like one big machine. From the inside it is a stack of decks, posts and tracks that all have to line up, or nothing loads the way it should. This trailer went through our shop for decking work, and the drone shows the part an owner rarely sees: the run under the upper decks, the frame tunnel from the rear to the belly, and the clearance above the tandem. Every one of those surfaces takes weight, vibration and wear on every single trip. Building decks that fit this structure is the whole job. Want work like this on your hauler? Car Hauler Repair Houston builds and installs decks in house.'
VO['insideframe']='insideframe.mp3'
S['rungear']='A car hauler can have a perfect frame and still be unsafe if the running gear underneath it is worn out. At Car Hauler Repair Houston we service suspension and running gear: shocks, brake chambers, drums, shoes, hubs, bearings, seals, wheels and tires. We pull hubs to check bearings and seals, look at the springs and mounts for cracks and movement, and replace what is out of service instead of sending it down the road for one more load. This is the part of the trailer that touches the highway, and it is the part inspectors look at first. Due for suspension or brake work? Car Hauler Repair Houston handles running gear along with everything else.'
VO['rungear']='rungear.mp3'
S['whyblast']='People ask why we blast a trailer instead of just painting over it. This is why. Old coatings and rust hold moisture against the steel, so anything sprayed on top starts failing from underneath on day one. Blasting takes the frame back to clean bare metal, which is the only surface a primer can really bond to, and it also shows us the truth about the steel: where it is solid and where it needs repair before any coating goes on. It is slow, it is dirty, and it is the reason the finish still looks right years later. Thinking about paint for your hauler? Start the conversation with Car Hauler Repair Houston.'
VO['whyblast']='whyblast.mp3'
S['warranty']='If you run a Cottrell, this one matters. Houston Car Hauler is a Cottrell Certified Warranty Repair Center, which means approved warranty and service work gets done here in Houston instead of being shipped somewhere else. We also work on Sun Country, Sun Valley, Wally-Mo, Boydstun, Miller, LOHR systems, stinger units and enclosed car haulers, from a single hydraulic hose to a complete frame reconstruction. Same shop, same team, whether the job is covered by warranty or not. Our goal is always the same: find the real damage, rebuild the structure properly, and put the equipment back to work. Cottrell owner in Texas? Car Hauler Repair Houston is your certified warranty shop.'
VO['warranty']='warranty.mp3'

# ===== 10 videos 2026-09-24 (scripts/topics_0924.txt) — [HOOK 2] marks the mid-video hook =====
S['deckdown']="Deck won't move? Line just blew and there's fluid on the pavement? The clock doesn't care, and neither does dispatch. At Car Hauler Repair Houston, car carriers are the only thing we work on. Burst lines and weeping fittings. Pumps and PTOs that spin but build nothing. Decks that creep halfway and quit, and cylinders that leak down overnight. Here's the part that saves your week: hoses are crimped right here and welding is done on site, so most of these failures turn the same day instead of waiting on a supplier. Cracked ramps, broken brackets, air leaks, brakes locked up on the scale. If it's on a car carrier, we fix it in this bay. Call the number on screen."
VO['deckdown']='deckdown.mp3'
HOOK['deckdown']=59
S['sameday']="Same failure. One day here, a week at the dealer. So what's the difference? At Car Hauler Repair Houston, four things line up. One: diagnosis starts on the phone, so we know what's coming before you pull in. Two: senior master techs who specialize in car carriers, not general trucks. Three: parts on hand, because hydraulic line and fittings are stocked, custom hoses are crimped in-house, and welding happens right here. And the fourth one surprises people. It's the price, fixed in writing before a wrench turns. Line all four up, in bays built for full-length multi-deck rigs, and most common carrier failures roll out the same day. Down right now? Call before you drive over."
VO['sameday']='sameday.mp3'
HOOK['sameday']=72
S['pricing']="How much does it cost just to find out what's wrong? Here, nothing. At Car Hauler Repair Houston you get a rough number on the phone, then an exact price in writing once the rig is inspected in the bay. Don't like the number? Take your keys and drive out owing zero. No diagnostic fee, no shop time, no inspection charge. Approve it, and we start right away, and nothing outside that price gets touched. And if we find something else halfway through? Work stops, you get a phone call, and you decide. No surprises on the invoice, and no number that moves after you agreed to it. You're already down. You should at least know the price. Call the number on screen."
VO['pricing']='pricing.mp3'
HOOK['pricing']=75
S['callfirst']="Sixty seconds on the phone can save your whole afternoon. When you call Car Hauler Repair Houston, you're not talking to a call center. Eugene, the shop director, picks up, asks what you're pulling and what quit, and diagnoses while you talk. He'll tell you straight whether to limp it in or get a tow, and whether there's a bay for you today. Want to cut that call in half? Have this ready: the brand and roughly how old it is, what quit, what it's doing, loaded or empty, and where the rig is right now. If Eugene is under a rig, send a text, and you'll hear back within fifteen minutes during shop hours. One call, and you know exactly where you stand."
VO['callfirst']='callfirst.mp3'
HOOK['callfirst']=63
S['loaded']="Your deck quits with cars still on it. Now what? The first thing most drivers ask us is whether we can take a rig loaded, and often the answer is yes. It depends on the failure and where the technician needs access, so tell us how many units you're carrying and where they sit, and we'll confirm on the call before you drive over. Why does that matter so much? Because unloading on the side of the road just to get a repair is a day you'll never get back. Our bays at Car Hauler Repair Houston are built for full-length multi-deck carriers, and if the job runs long, your rig sits securely behind our gate overnight instead of on an open shoulder. Loaded and down? Call us first."
VO['loaded']='loaded.mp3'
HOOK['loaded']=64
S['bays']="Most truck shops were built for trucks. Ours was built for car carriers. Car Hauler Repair Houston runs four full-service bays sized for full-length multi-deck rigs, so your trailer comes all the way inside instead of waiting in a yard. We're in southeast Houston, off the Gulf Freeway, about a mile and a half from the I forty-five and six ten interchange, and just minutes from America's Auto Auction. What does that mean for you? No more hunting for a shop that can actually fit your rig. Four bays, first come, first served, Monday through Saturday, seven in the morning to six at night. Call or text before you roll in, and we'll tell you if a bay is open."
VO['bays']='bays.mp3'
HOOK['bays']=73
S['reviews']="Five stars from twenty-five Google reviews, and they keep saying the same things. One carrier owner had the rear arms replaced and all the welding handled, and called the quality top-notch and the pricing more than fair. Another had a rear deck repaired and noticed that everything lined up and operated correctly, because the job was done right instead of patched. So what do customers mention most? Clear estimates, and reports that explain what's being done and why, so they feel confident leaving their truck with us. One driver was in and out within a couple of hours after a single phone call. Read all twenty-five reviews on Google, then call Car Hauler Repair Houston."
VO['reviews']='reviews.mp3'
HOOK['reviews']=63
S['fleet']="Running a fleet, not just one truck? Then the best time to call us is before a unit goes down. Fleet managers who have already talked to Eugene at Car Hauler Repair Houston get a faster read when a carrier breaks, because we already know the equipment. The pricing policy is the same for one rig or twenty: an exact price in writing, and nothing extra without your approval. Here's what fleet owners like most: we take the cards your drivers already carry, Comchek, EFS and T-Chek, plus cash and every major card. Most common failures turn the same day, and if a job runs long, the rig stays secure behind our gate overnight. Keep your fleet loading. Call before you're broken."
VO['fleet']='fleet.mp3'
HOOK['fleet']=69
S['warranty6']="What happens if a repair doesn't hold? At Car Hauler Repair Houston, completed repairs come with a six-month warranty on labor and workmanship. If something we did doesn't hold, bring it back, and we make it right. Cottrell warranty repairs are a separate story, because they carry Cottrell's own coverage. And here's the honest part: sometimes a rig just needs to get home. Anything we flag as a temporary or limp-it-home fix is called out up front, before you pay, so you always know which repairs are covered and which ones are a stopgap. No fine print discovered later. Just a straight answer, a price in writing, and work that's backed. Call the number on screen."
VO['warranty6']='warranty6.mp3'
HOOK['warranty6']=51
S['cottrell']="Own a Cottrell? Where you repair it can decide whether your warranty survives. Cottrell's limited warranty does not apply if the trailer is modified or repaired by anyone other than Cottrell or its authorized representatives. Car Hauler Repair Houston is a Cottrell authorized warranty repair center, right here in Houston. So how does it work? Cottrell approves the claim and issues a work order before any repair starts, and the covered work is done in our bay, without the dealer's week-long queue. On new units, the coverage itself comes from Cottrell: thirty-six months on the mainframe structure, wear items excluded, and twelve months on Cottrell-made hydraulic cylinders. Keep your warranty intact. Bring your Cottrell to Car Hauler Repair Houston."
VO['cottrell']='cottrell.mp3'
HOOK['cottrell']=50
